    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="65443ffa-a72a-5e10-b595-dbaeed4a0cc7" activityNameId="87831d04-7618-5aac-8c90-1faf99765b56" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, decarbonising waste, 30% water, to residual material landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, decarbonising waste, 30% water, to residual material landfill
Inventoried waste contains 100% decarbonising waste; . waste composition (wet, in ppm): H2O 300000; O 469000; H n.a.; C n.a.; S 1866.7; N 770; P 840.49; B n.a.; Cl 192.5; Br n.a.; F n.a.; I n.a.; Ag n.a.; As 3.85; Ba n.a.; Cd 1.0605; Co n.a.; Cr 19.25; Cu 29.75; Hg 0.1785; Mn n.a.; Mo n.a.; Ni 18.2; Pb 29.75; Sb n.a.; Se n.a.; Sn n.a.; V n.a.; Zn 77; Be n.a.; Sc n.a.; Sr n.a.; Ti n.a.; Tl n.a.; W n.a.; Si 10634; Fe 13954; Ca 187610; Al 4816.1; K 639.22; Mg 9498.8; Na n.a.; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 60.4%. ;; UUID: 32cefe22-dac9-45c6-8c49-c14cc6e7610d
Waste-specific short-term emissions to water from leachate. Long-term emissions from landfill to ground water. 
Location: Technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Landfill includes base seal and leachate collection system.
Technology: Swiss residual material landfill for polluted, inorganic waste. With base seal and leachate collection system. Recultivation after closure. 
Time period: Waste composition as given in literature reference, theoretical data or other source. Transfer coefficients from prospective model.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Landfill model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial waste composition from various literature sources. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_32cefe22-dac9-45c6-8c49-c14cc6e7610d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
